<title>SWEDEN: Sweden's Riksbank board meeting ends, no changes.</title>
<headline>Sweden's Riksbank board meeting ends, no changes.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's central bank, the Riksbank, ended a board meeting by telephone on Thursday with no announcement to changes to interest rates.</p>
<p>The market had not expected the Riksbank to make any changes.</p>
<p>The Riksbank's key interest rate, the repo rate, currently stands at 4.10 percent. It was last lowered on December 17.</p>
<p>Its other key rates, the deposit and lending rates, stand at 3.75 percent and 5.25 percent, respectively.</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
